xrt-smi platform report and the power-mode knob -- Desktop 2 (Phoenix, Ryzen 7 8700G),
2026-09-07. Driver 32.0.20101.3760, xrt-smi from C:\Windows\System32\AMD\xrt-smi.exe, run
with --batch so the output carries no terminal escape codes.

Not a benchmark. A verbatim capture of what the driver's own tool reports about this NPU,
recorded because docs/SILICON.md cites two things from it that no earlier log carried: the
"Power Mode" field of the platform report, and the list of modes `xrt-smi configure
--pmode` accepts. Nothing on the device was changed -- --pmode was not exercised, only its
help was printed. "Total Columns: 5" is the same reading docs/DECISIONS.md first recorded
(results/aie/aiecompiler_part_phoenix_candidate.log:29 quotes it), repeated here so the
three facts sit in one log.

Note the report prints no clock frequency of any kind. The AIE core clock this repo
cites (1.6 GHz for the 8700G, RESEARCH.md, from a web search) is not measured by anything
on this machine yet; docs/SILICON.md objective S0 is that measurement.

=== xrt-smi --batch examine -r platform ===

-----------------------------
[003d:00:01.1] : NPU Phoenix
-----------------------------
Platform
  Name                   : NPU Phoenix
  Power Mode             : Default
  Total Columns          : 5

Estimated Power          : N/A

=== xrt-smi --batch configure --help ===

COMMAND: configure

DESCRIPTION: Device and host configuration.

USAGE: xrt-smi configure [-h] [-d arg] [--pmode arg]

OPTIONS:
  -d, --device       - The Bus:Device.Function (e.g., 0000:d8:00.0) device of interest
  -h, --help         - Help to use this sub-command
  --pmode            - Modes: default, powersaver, balanced, performance, turbo


GLOBAL OPTIONS:
  --verbose          - Turn on verbosity
  --batch            - Enable batch mode (disables escape characters)
  --force            - When possible, force an operation

=== xrt-smi examine --help, report types this driver offers (from the same session) ===

  -r, --report       - The type of report to be produced. Reports currently available are:
                         aie-partitions - AIE partition information
                         all            - All known reports are produced
                         host           - Host information
                         platform       - Platforms flashed on the device

No "clocks" or "telemetry" report exists on this driver version; aie-partitions is the
report tools/session_hold.py and tools/multi_partition_bench.py already read.
